cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  To cite the mathematics, cite the paper (preferred citation below). To cite
  the formalization itself, cite this repository.
title: "The speed of biased random walk on leafless Bienaymé trees is monotone: Lean formalization assuming the interval verifications of Appendix A"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kortchemski
    given-names: Igor
repository-code: https://github.com/igor-kortchemski/monotonicity-speed-biased-random-walk-palomar
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formalization
  - biased random walk
  - Bienaymé trees
  - speed
  - computer-assisted proof
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of Theorem 1.1 of "The speed of biased
  random walk on leafless Bienaymé trees is monotone" by ChatGPT, directed by
  Igor Kortchemski (Hexagon 2611.00820), assuming the statements that the two
  interval verifications of its Appendix A check: the speed of the biased random
  walk on a leafless Bienaymé tree is C^1 and strictly decreasing on [0, m). Only
  the axioms propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound are used. The two
  statements are proved in the companion repository
  monotonicity-speed-biased-random-walk. Produced with AI agents; the Lean
  kernel checks the proofs.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  authors:
